# ==============================================================================
# CoopIS - Enterprise Cooperative Management Information System
# Environment Configuration & Deployment Reference
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. LOCAL DOCKER COMPOSE CONFIGURATION
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PostgreSQL Database Settings
POSTGRES_DB=coopis_db
POSTGRES_USER=postgres
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgrespassword
POSTGRES_PORT=5432

# .NET Web API Settings
API_PORT=5208
ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production
ENABLE_SWAGGER=true

# Database Connection (Inter-container connection string)
DATABASE_URL=Host=db;Port=5432;Database=coopis_db;Username=postgres;Password=postgrespassword

# JWT Authentication Secret (Must be >= 256 bits / 32 characters in production)
JWT_SECRET=CoopIS_Super_Secure_Secret_Key_For_Jwt_Token_Generation_2026_Enterprise!
JWT_ISSUER=CoopIS.Api
JWT_AUDIENCE=CoopIS.Client

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. DEFAULT SEEDED CREDENTIALS (Created automatically by DbInitializer on startup)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Administrator: username: admin     | password: Admin123!   (Full privileges)
# Regular User:  username: loanuser  | password: User123!    (Member/Loans view only)

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. CLOUD DEPLOYMENT BLUEPRINTS
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- A. AWS ECS (FARGATE) + AWS RDS POSTGRESQL + AWS SECRETS MANAGER ---
# 1. Provision RDS PostgreSQL 16 (db.t4g.micro for dev, db.r6g.large for prod).
# 2. Store secrets in AWS Secrets Manager:
#    - DATABASE_URL: Host=coopis-prod.xxxx.ap-southeast-1.rds.amazonaws.com;Port=5432;Database=coopis_db;Username=coop_admin;Password=<RDS_PASSWORD>;SSL Mode=Require;
#    - JWT_SECRET: <64-character-cryptographically-random-hex-string>
# 3. Push Docker images to Amazon ECR:
#    - docker tag coopis-api:latest <ACCOUNT_ID>.dkr.ecr.ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com/coopis-api:v1.0
#    - docker tag coopis-web:latest <ACCOUNT_ID>.dkr.ecr.ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com/coopis-web:v1.0
# 4. In ECS Task Definition:
#    - Map secrets from Secrets Manager to container environment variables:
#      DATABASE_URL -> secretsManager:coopis/prod/db:DATABASE_URL::
#      JWT_SECRET   -> secretsManager:coopis/prod/jwt:JWT_SECRET::
# 5. Set up an Application Load Balancer (ALB):
#    - Listener 443 with ACM SSL Certificate
#    - Path /api/* forwards to API Target Group (Port 8080)
#    - Default * forwards to Web/Nginx Target Group (Port 80)

# --- B. AZURE APP SERVICE + AZURE POSTGRESQL FLEXIBLE SERVER ---
# 1. Create Azure Database for PostgreSQL Flexible Server.
# 2. Create Azure Key Vault and store:
#    - ConnectionStrings--CoopDbConnection: Host=coopis-server.postgres.database.azure.com;Port=5432;Database=coopis_db;Username=coopadmin;Password=<AZURE_PASS>;SSL Mode=Require;
#    - Jwt--Key: <Azure-Secured-JWT-Signing-Key>
# 3. Create Azure App Service (Linux Container) or Azure Container Apps:
#    - Reference Key Vault values in App Service configuration:
#      @Microsoft.KeyVault(SecretUri=https://coopis-vault.vault.azure.net/secrets/CoopDbConnection/...)
# 4. Bind Custom Domain with Free Managed SSL Certificate.

# --- C. RENDER / SUPABASE / NEON (QUICK PAAS LAUNCH) ---
# 1. Supabase / Neon: Create a free PostgreSQL project and copy the connection string:
#    DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@db.[PROJECT-REF].supabase.co:5432/postgres?sslmode=require
# 2. Render.com:
#    - Web Service 1 (API): Point to root directory, Dockerfile: Dockerfile.api
#      Add Environment Variables:
#        DATABASE_URL = <Supabase/Neon URI>
#        JWT_SECRET   = <Your Secret Key>
#        ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT = Production
#    - Web Service 2 (Frontend): Point to root directory, Dockerfile: Dockerfile.web
#      Add Environment Variable or configure Nginx proxy to point to Render API service URL.
